cy9BLTg3NjAt/MTY3MzgwOTA4My04/ODg0LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"American singer, entertainer, songwriter, actress, producer, director and businesswoman born August 16, 1958 in Bay City, Michigan. After performing in the music groups [a=Breakfast Club] and [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/Emmy+(7)]Emmy[/url], she signed with [l=Sire] in 1982 and released her debut album \"[m=5319]\" the following year.\r\nShe subsequently released a series of commercially successful albums, has sold more than 400 million records worldwide, and is recognized by Guinness World Records as the best-selling female recording artist of all time. Madonna has been honorifically dubbed — and is widely recognized as — “the Queen of Pop.��\r\nShe was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in her first year of eligibility. She was also ranked number one on VH1’s 100 Greatest Women in Music list and number two on Billboard’s Greatest Hot 100 Artists of All Time (behind only the Beatles), making her the most successful solo artist in the history of the American singles chart.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:8760","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":3250793,"name":"Lulu Smith"},{"id":3424607,"name":"Madonna Louise Ciccone"},{"id":12127411,"name":"Madonna Ritchie"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Ciccone Madona","Donna","M","MDNA","Mad","Mad On Her 2","Mad-Donna","MadDonna","Mada","Madana","Maddona","Madna","Madnna","Madona","Madonna '86","Madonnan","Madonne","Madoona","Modonna","Queen Of Pop - 瑪丹娜","Мадона","Мадонна","מדונה","マドンナ","世紀女皇瑪丹娜","瑪丹娜","麥丹娜","麥當娜","麦当娜","마돈나"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/8760-Madonna","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.madonna.com","http://www.allmusic.com/artist/madonna-mn0000237205","http://www.dailymotion.com/madonnaofficial","http://www.facebook.com/madonna","http://www.flickr.com/photos/madonnaphotos","http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0000187","http://www.instagram.com/madonna","http://linktr.ee/madonna","http://www.snapchat.com/@madonna","http://soundcloud.com/madonna","http://www.tiktok.com/@madonna","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna","http://x.com/Madonna","http://www.youtube.com/@madonna"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/90254/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"90254","image":"https://i.discogs.com/V7f91Z1YTxHh5OjiteRxE3clfEOLG4YPSsrdtSEm-Q0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:550/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTkwMjU0/LTE3ODM0MDEyNjgt/MjEwMC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/YcHlh6Q_I01HzRBSWCdUYOQ0LDSQwpOyw0aE8kaB-ME/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTkwMjU0/LTE3ODM0MDEyNjgt/MjEwMC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"American singer and keyboardist, born January 19, 1956 in Youngstown, Ohio - died April 5, 2023.\r\n\r\nHe was a member of the Philly soul group Sweet Thunder which had a hit with “Baby I Need Your Love Today” and a handful of moderately successful albums on the Fantasy label. From there Newberry briefly joined the dance group Impact before embarking on a solo career.\r\n\r\nSigned to Neil Bogart's Boardwalk label, Newberry worked on his solo debut with producers Bobby Eli and Nick Martinelli. His song “Love Town” became an international hit.\r\n\r\nNewberry continued to record from time to time with less success through the 1980s and 1990s, later landing on the Malaco blues label.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:90254","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":232929,"name":"Sweet Thunder"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["B. Newberry","B. Newberry III","Booker Newberey III","Booker Newberry","Booker Newberry !!!","Booker Newberry 111","Booker Newberry 3rd","Booker Newbury 111","Booker Newbury III","Booker T. Newberry","Booker T. Newberry III","Booker T. Newberry, III","Brooker Newberry","Brooker Newberry III","Newberry"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/90254-Booker-Newberry-III","type":"artist","urls":["http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Newberry_II